* 5.0.0
    - Rewrote client support for currently live classic talent-tree versions: Classic Era / Hardcore / Season of Discovery (Interface 11509) and Burning Crusade Classic Anniversary (Interface 20506)
    - Added Core/Compat.lua for C_AddOns, spell info, and TooltipDataProcessor-compatible spell tooltips
    - Added Core/Flavor.lua for ruleset detection and talent point level lookup
    - Replaced fragile ToggleTalentFrame-only init with ADDON_LOADED / PLAYER_LOGIN talent UI attachment
    - Reject imports built for a different Classic ruleset than the current client
    - Updated README and packaging notes for the live Classic clients

* 3.2.3
    - Renamed the active sequence button from Load to Manage
    - Renamed the import action to Import URL for clearer sequence management UI
    - Updated the import dialog prompt to explicitly request a Wowhead talent URL

* 3.2.2
    - Moved saved talent sequences to an account-wide library
    - Added automatic migration from legacy per-character saved sequences
    - Grouped imported sequences by class in the sequence browser
    - Pinned the current character class to the top of the list
    - Disabled loading sequences for classes other than the logged-in character
    - Read the target class directly from Wowhead URLs during import

* 3.2.1
    - Reorganized the addon into a clean top-level Classic/TBC source layout
    - Added flavor-specific Vanilla and TBC TOCs
    - Fixed StaticPopup import dialog compatibility on current Classic clients
    - Fixed deleting the active sequence so it no longer returns as <unnamed> on reload
    - Reworked Wowhead parsing to use explicit flavor/class/tree talent-name mappings
    - Added mapped Wowhead support for all TBC classes
    - Removed deprecated Icy Veins import support
    - Updated packaging and README for the cleaned source tree

